course: dictionary
lesson: 5784
title: Lymph in the body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lymph is a clear, watery fluid that moves around your body through thin tubes. You may not see it, but it is always flowing, like a quiet river that carries things to where they are needed.
explain: Lymph carries white blood cells, and these cells fight germs. The example sentence shows this: «Lymph nodes, often called glands, are part of the immune system and swell while fighting an infection, such as in the neck during a cold.» When the nodes swell, your body is working hard against germs.
explain: The words around lymph give you clues. It sits next to nodes, system and tubes, so it must be a body fluid that moves through the body. Test it by swapping in the word fluid: «lymph nodes» becomes «fluid nodes», so you know lymph is a kind of fluid.
fact: Lymph is a clear, watery fluid.
fact: Lymph moves around the body in thin tubes.
fact: Lymph carries white blood cells that fight germs.
fact: «Lymph nodes» are often called glands, and they can swell when you have an infection.
fact: The lymphatic system is the network of tubes and parts that carries lymph around the body.
exercise: «Lymph is a clear, watery fluid that moves around the body.» What is lymph? | *A clear, watery fluid that moves around the body | A loud noise made by the heart | A kind of cough medicine | A hard bone in the arm
exercise: «Lymph nodes swell while fighting an infection, such as in the neck during a cold.» Why might your neck swell during a cold? | Your neck has become too cold | Your bones are growing | You have eaten too much cake | *The lymph nodes in your neck are fighting germs
exercise: Lymph nodes are often called what? | *Glands | Bones | Hairs | Muscles
test: Lymph carries white blood cells. What do these cells do? | Carry food to the stomach | Hold the bones together | *Fight germs | Make the skin change colour
test: Lymph moves around the body in thin tubes. What does the word tubes suggest about how lymph travels? | Lymph sits still in one place | Lymph is stored in the ears | Lymph flies through the air | *Lymph flows along narrow pipe-like paths
exam: Why might a doctor check the lymph nodes in your neck when you are ill? | Because they make you grow taller | *Because they can swell when your body is fighting an infection | Because they are the same thing as your ears | Because they hold your teeth in place
